    "created_at": "2017-10-16T18:00:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-16T18:00:36Z",
    "body": "> I think instead this should be on the heading \"Path2D objects\". That's what I did in similar situations in the workers section.\r\n\r\nThe problem with that is, the link at https://caniuse.com/#feat=path2d is specifically to the fragment `#dom-Path2D`, which goes to the ID for the `Path2D()` constructor, while the heading \"Path2D objects\" references the ID `Path2D`, which is for a different ID (the `Path2D` object’s ID).\r\n\r\nSo just putting the `subdfn` on the heading \"Path2D objects\" won’t fix the build error and won’t allow the caniuse annotation to show up in the dev edition — unless we do this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n-  <h6><code>Path2D</code> objects</h6>\r\n+  <h6><code subdfn data-x=\"dom-Path2D\">Path2D</code> objects</h6>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat is, also add `data-x=\"dom-Path2D\"` to it.\r\n\r\nBut that doesn’t seem right because of course it’s taking that heading from being a reference to the `Path2D` object and changing it to being a reference to the `Path2D()` constructor.",
